 {
  "type": "post",
  "id": "7498387201869651968",
  "linkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/bonardglobal_affordability-regulation-shifting-demand-activity-7498387201869651968-m7Dk",
  "content": "Affordability, regulation, shifting demand and student flows are putting pressure on the UK PBSA market, but the impact varies significantly.\n\nTo provide a clearer view of these market conditions, BONARD has prepared a more comprehensive UK PBSA Market Report, supported by extensive data, field intelligence and expert analysis.\n\nJoin BONARD for the report launch webinar, featuring a presentation of the key findings and an expert panel discussion.\n\nThe webinar will cover:\n\u2022 Expert views from six top executives\n\u2022 Key findings from the UK PBSA Market Report 2026\n\u2022 Analysis of 113 UK markets\n\u2022 New student demand data\n\u2022 755,000 PBSA beds in operation\n\u2022 176,000 PBSA beds in development\n\u2022 285 UK PBSA transactions\n\u2022 BTR and co-living sector data\n\u2022 Gross and net provision rates\n\u2022 New detail on rents and yields\n\u2022 Market trends and forecasts\n\nMartin Varga, Chief Growth Officer at BONARD, will present the report\u2019s key findings before Samuel Vetrak, MRICS, CEO of BONARD, chairs a panel discussion with:\n\u2022 Alex Pease CEO, Watkin Jones Group\n\u2022 Stewart Moore, CEO, Host.\n\u2022 Nigel A. Allsopp, Managing Director, Investment Strategy & Research, Greystar\n\u2022 Philip Wedge Bernal, Director, European Research, Harrison Street Asset Management\n\nWednesday, 2 September 2026\n2:00 PM BST | 3:00 PM CET | 9:00 AM EDT\n\nRegister for the webinar here:\nhttps://lnkd.in/exhmv-dB",
