 {
  "type": "post",
  "id": "7500911707658145792",
  "linkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/cushman-%26-wakefield_global-construction-costs-are-stabilizing-activity-7500911707658145792-PfiS",
  "content": "Global construction costs are stabilizing on some fronts, even as energy and metals markets stay volatile. Metals prices climbed 6.2% quarter-over-quarter (QOQ) in Q2 2026, reflecting continued demand tied to electrification and data center growth, while labor cost growth has cooled from recent peaks.\n\nMaterials and equipment are now leading the sector's cost story, with strong demand fundamentals \u2013 including a forecast global refined copper deficit \u2013 pointing to sustained investment in infrastructure and grid modernization through 2026.\n\nDiscover how these trends may shape your 2026 strategy in our latest Construction Insights for Global Occupiers report >> https://cushwk.co/4wZ2WPN",
