 {
  "type": "post",
  "id": "7500993985268563968",
  "linkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/starrez_the-hidden-link-between-ai-strategy-and-student-activity-7500993985268563968-Sgd2",
  "content": "What if the real opportunity with AI in higher education isn\u2019t just greater efficiency, but stronger student connection?\n\nIn a new article for eCampus News, StarRez Executive Chairman Travis Knipe and Shirley M. Collado, Ph.D., President & CEO of College Track, explore the important connection between AI strategy, the student living experience, and retention.\n\nTheir perspective: the most effective AI strategies start with a real student or staff challenge, not the technology itself. Used thoughtfully, AI can help teams identify where students may need support, reduce administrative burden, and create more capacity for the human relationships that help students feel connected and thrive.\n\nAs higher education continues navigating AI adoption, keeping the student experience at the center will be critical.\n\nRead the full article below \ud83d\udc47\n\nhttps://lnkd.in/g9cg_uuH",
